LOAD BALANCER

--- DevOps Roles & Responsibilities ---

- Set up and manage development, testing, and production environments.
- Build application code and create Docker images for deployment.
- Deploy containerized applications and packages across environments.
- Execute and manage database SQL scripts for application releases.
- Configure and maintain system configuration parameters.
- Perform database backup and restoration to ensure data reliability.
- Maintain system security, access control, and environment compliance.
- Manage system patching and regular security updates.
- Manage user access and permissions across infrastructure and systems.
- Design and implement CI/CD pipelines for automated deployments.
- Document environment architecture, configurations, and operational procedures.
- Collaborate with developers to troubleshoot and resolve application issues.
- Monitor server performance metrics (CPU, memory, JVM utilization).
- Perform regular housekeeping tasks including log cleanup, reports, Docker images, and database maintenance.
- Maintain environment inventory including server specs, IPs, repositories, pipelines, and domain details.
- Implement and manage performance monitoring and observability tools.
- Troubleshoot and resolve infrastructure and environment-related issues.
- Communicate environment updates and changes with project stakeholders.
- Follow operational processes, release procedures, and deployment checklists.
- Track and resolve assigned tasks, incidents, and service requests.


